<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian Civil War (1432–1438)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1432–1438</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian Civil War of 1432–1438 was fought over the throne of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svitrigaila">Švitrigaila</a> and Sigismund Kęstutaitis, who was backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Sigismund's victory at Pabaiskas (Wiłkomierz) in 1435 decided the war in his favour and kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> in its union with Poland, though Sigismund himself was murdered in 1440.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-civil-war-1432-1438.jpg" alt="Lithuanian Civil War (1432–1438)" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: en:User:Orionus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vilkamir_battle_monument_%E2%80%94_%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BD%D1%96%D0%BA_%D0%B1%D1%96%D1%82%D0%B2%D1%8B_%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%B4_%D0%92%D1%96%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC.Jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
